{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve DNSSEC-signed authoritative zone infra.test with node1 as primary, node2/node3 as secondaries, app.infra.test resolving to node1's service address, and status.infra.test TXT equal to ready.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final direct observations show node1 as a secure, inline-signing primary and node2/node3 as secure secondaries, all synchronized at serial 2026090106. Each returns the required A and TXT records, DNSKEY, and signed answers; node4 receives AD-validated responses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e200038331024f7b","cmd-321631edd3434e1b","cmd-d9075c7fc8d24616","cmd-db51065ecf5d4a4e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node4 to resolve through both secondary authoritative servers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node4 persistently lists both secondary addresses. A normal query used node2, while the bounded node2 outage caused subsequent queries to use node3, directly demonstrating use of both paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cacbf95124d14837","cmd-e91a8478aa6a4fcc","cmd-db51065ecf5d4a4e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Support authenticated DNS updates from node1 and propagate accepted changes to both secondaries.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A TSIG-authenticated update issued from node1 after its reboot was accepted, signed, and advanced the zone to serial 2026090106. Both secondaries then directly returned that serial and the new signed value, and node4 validated it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-55a12c0162aa48dc","cmd-321631edd3434e1b","cmd-d9075c7fc8d24616","cmd-db51065ecf5d4a4e"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep resolution available through one authoritative-server outage and recover the disrupted server afterward.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both secondaries had a healthy synchronized baseline. Node2 was then stopped with its DNS listener confirmed absent; node4 still resolved the required records through node3 and obtained an AD-validated answer after cache flush. Node2 was restored active, enabled, synchronized, and serving signed data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-16ce8a4dd60e4d96","cmd-eeff0f47c61d450c","cmd-a9deb185783747f8","cmd-e91a8478aa6a4fcc","cmd-fe76e8339ef74d4f"]},{"id":"P1","requirement":"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol (independent assurance check, not a public task requirement).","status":"satisfied","summary":"Every managed node has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service and DNS data. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's before/after identities. Node2's transient connection reset occurred during reboot and was followed by a successful complete recovery observation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9a97b118a4ab4e0c","cmd-98ee7b2ed3e2470f","cmd-9d9d41d304824fa4","cmd-ee5a0ecbe33b4040","cmd-7183f82ba8884b52","cmd-1f0911d30ee04a27","cmd-b6c40911771e4eec","cmd-04a15ca070094156","cmd-01670b9dc47b4292","cmd-cacbf95124d14837","cmd-f52068e86ace455f","cmd-aa9aa47b71784657","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No executor-caused hygiene defect is evident. All nodes finish without failed services and with healthy package-manager consistency. New port-53 listeners are the intended BIND services, and the TSIG key has restricted root:named 0640 permissions.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets","cmd-e200038331024f7b"]},"overall_summary":"All four material public-task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent behavioral evidence. DNSSEC authority, required records, dual-secondary resolution, authenticated update propagation, bounded outage continuity, restoration, and final synchronized state were all observed. The independent restart protocol is also complete and lifecycle-consistent on every managed node.","limitations":[]}
